WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.288
The technical documentation - for anyone

00:00:03.348 --> 00:00:06.706
who authors tools, integrates Lolly into a

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.114
pipeline, self-hosts it, or extends the

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.494
platform.

00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:14.819
What's in it for you.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:18.520
Build a tool once and the request stops

00:00:18.583 --> 00:00:20.593
coming back to you.

00:00:21.372 --> 00:00:25.169
The repetitive "can you just make me a…"

00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:28.475
that eats your afternoons becomes a

00:00:28.565 --> 00:00:31.034
template other people fill in themselves -

00:00:31.095 --> 00:00:34.269
correctly, without you in the loop.

00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:39.845
Your work is plain HTML/CSS/JS:

00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:42.321
version-controlled, diffable, reviewable

00:00:42.385 --> 00:00:45.018
and running on an open engine with no

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:48.544
vendor lock-in, so it stays yours.

00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:52.121
Automate the production run and your time

00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:55.023
goes to the interesting problem, not the

00:00:55.103 --> 00:00:57.319
ten-thousandth export.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:09.900
Lolly is a platform-agnostic engine that runs the same render path across several shells «web PWA, Tauri desktop/mobile, CLI, TUI».

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:20.625
Tools are data, not bundled code - a manifest plus a template plus optional hooks - so new tools ship without an app update.

00:01:20.975 --> 00:01:28.475
Start with the Overview for the architecture, then follow the track that fits what you're building.

00:01:29.241 --> 00:01:31.969
New to the platform?

00:01:32.731 --> 00:01:35.579
The Quickstart gets a brand and your first

00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:38.644
render in place before you go deep.

00:01:39.025 --> 00:01:42.700
You're the multiplier in the relay.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:02:05.300
A creative authors a template «Lolly for Creators»; you take that exact tool and scale it - into a pipeline, a CLI batch or an MCP endpoint - so a non-designer can self-serve the finished asset offline, and an AI agent can run it at a volume no person would sit through.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:11.150
See how your work slots into The lifecycle of a campaign.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.945
Understand the architecture

00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:18.493
Overview - why Lolly exists, the

00:02:18.587 --> 00:02:22.448
engine/shell/tools separation, the

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.769
capability bridge and the settled

00:02:24.855 --> 00:02:27.019
architectural commitments.

00:02:27.785 --> 00:02:31.236
Design Tokens - the DTCG token model

00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:34.374
brands are expressed in, and how tools

00:02:34.435 --> 00:02:35.994
consume them.

00:02:37.127 --> 00:02:38.879
Author tools

00:02:39.847 --> 00:02:43.175
Every control below was generated from a

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:46.170
declared input in tool-json.

00:02:46.943 --> 00:02:49.471
You write the manifest line, the host

00:02:49.531 --> 00:02:52.496
draws the widget and the same model drives

00:02:52.546 --> 00:02:55.045
the CLI and the URL.

00:02:55.816 --> 00:02:59.518
That scales further than five controls.

00:03:00.286 --> 00:03:03.378
Give an input a section and the host folds

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:06.891
it away, so a fifty-input tool like Chart

00:03:06.966 --> 00:03:10.349
still opens as a short stack with the rest

00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:12.969
filed behind named groups.

00:03:13.731 --> 00:03:16.041
Authoring Tools - the full guide:

00:03:16.121 --> 00:03:18.710
manifest, template, styles, hooks,

00:03:18.771 --> 00:03:21.094
composition and publishing.

00:03:21.862 --> 00:03:24.830
Authoring Assets - catalog assets, tiers,

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.568
locales, palettes, themable icons and

00:03:27.657 --> 00:03:28.744
fonts.

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:43.325
Host API - the HostV1 capability bridge every tool is written against «the portable API tools are written against - note hooks are not sandboxed, see Authoring Tools».

00:03:44.091 --> 00:03:48.407
URL Mode - every input as a URL parameter;

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.312
reserved params, compact encoding, packed

00:03:51.374 --> 00:03:52.419
links.

00:03:53.559 --> 00:03:55.810
Run & integrate

00:03:56.757 --> 00:03:59.555
CLI - headless rendering; the same render

00:03:59.624 --> 00:04:04.244
path as the GUI, driven by --foo=bar argv.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.419
TUI - the interactive terminal shell.

00:04:09.184 --> 00:04:12.643
MCP Server - the native endpoint that lets

00:04:12.732 --> 00:04:16.619
an AI agent discover and run tools.

00:04:17.393 --> 00:04:20.961
AI Agents - driving Lolly from a model: a

00:04:21.043 --> 00:04:23.794
URL is the API.

00:04:24.562 --> 00:04:28.321
Chrome Extension - capture a live URL as a

00:04:28.385 --> 00:04:30.268
reusable asset.

00:04:31.423 --> 00:04:33.598
Ship & operate it

00:04:34.556 --> 00:04:37.223
Build Guide - build every target: CLI,

00:04:37.304 --> 00:04:39.719
TUI, desktop, mobile.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.974
Deployment - the web app, the apps and the

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.594
backend services; where each piece runs.

00:04:47.347 --> 00:04:50.507
Configuration - profiles, brand packs,

00:04:50.569 --> 00:04:53.114
capability gating, feature flags and

00:04:53.177 --> 00:04:55.195
catalog validation.

00:04:56.302 --> 00:04:58.399
Trust & data

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.415
Rights and authorship are inputs like any

00:05:02.465 --> 00:05:03.394
other.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.233
Embed & Track Image declares creator,

00:05:07.304 --> 00:05:10.970
copyright, licence and contact fields, and

00:05:11.005 --> 00:05:13.854
the export writes them into the file's own

00:05:13.914 --> 00:05:17.619
metadata and its C2PA manifest.

00:05:18.373 --> 00:05:21.526
Content Credentials Identity - CA-issued

00:05:21.595 --> 00:05:24.978
signing for on-device C2PA; engine

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:27.970
contracts and the operator runbook.

00:05:28.741 --> 00:05:31.832
Data Transfer - the lolly-backup bundle:

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.325
envelope, integrity and cross-shell

00:05:34.386 --> 00:05:35.869
guarantees.

00:05:36.644 --> 00:05:39.712
About - the project, its licence boundary

00:05:39.809 --> 00:05:41.719
and the repository.
